cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Lattice Theta Functions with Half-Integral Characteristics"
abstract: >-
  Exact proofs, certificates, and reproducible computations for identical
  vanishing of lattice theta functions with half-integral characteristics.
  The symmetry converse holds in ranks one through three and fails in rank
  four. Rank-four results: an identically vanishing even characteristic of a
  lattice of determinant 1729 whose two coset lattices are the Conway-Sloane
  isospectral pair, which are not isometric, and the smallest such zero, of
  determinant 280; the minimum determinant of a rank-four counterexample to
  the symmetry converse is 280, by complete isometry-class lists through
  determinant 279 with independent replays; an even counterexample of
  determinant 1156 with automorphism group {I, -I}, the minimum of its
  Eisenstein family; and the rank-four parity property, which fails for
  indecomposable odd lattices of determinant 49 not divisible by four and
  for even indecomposable lattices of odd determinant at determinant 121,
  with complete class lists and structural theorems; for even indecomposable
  lattices of odd determinant, every symmetry zero comes from a square root
  of -I, any zero of determinant 5 mod 8 would have to be a pair of
  isospectral non-isometric coset lattices, and complete class lists through
  determinant 501 contain no other zeros; release 1.4.0 proves that no such
  zero exists at any determinant (Theorem S, a computer-assisted
  classification over Voronoi's primitive cones of quaternary forms), so
  every vanishing nontrivial even characteristic of an even rank-four
  lattice of odd determinant is a symmetry zero. The release also
  includes the low-rank parity classification, the irreducible
  crystallographic root lattices in the stated normalization, exact
  determinant-at-most-24 censuses through rank four, and a checked
  literature note on isospectral lattices. No literature-priority claim is
  made.
